id: pm-github-samq
title: Coordinate caller adoption and source-content remediation for scheduled workflows
description: "Current adoption scope: the November 6 watch covers 21 failing sync runs and 15 failing closeout runs across 22 public callers. Start with the complete per-caller matrix and required actions in docs/scheduled-workflow-watch-1106.md. Historical context: After pm-github-3it2 is released, update affected reusable workflow SHA pins through caller-owned review. All 21 named caller repositories are listed in docs/scheduled-workflow-refusals.md. Align newline required-checks declarations where GITHUB_TOKEN cannot read administration-only protection. pm-changelog sync job 121514139043 also requires source-content remediation or a reviewed narrow allowlist for absolute-host-path body findings; package diagnostics must preserve that refusal. No caller mutation belongs to the package fix."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: caller-adoption,closeout,follow-up,sync
created_at: "2026-10-27T03:39:19.756Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T08:49:18.379Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Caller owners adopt a release containing the pagination/diagnostic fix, review required-check declarations against branch policy, and resolve source privacy findings. Validate each scheduled workflow under its real GITHUB_TOKEN without weakening evidence or privacy gates."
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T15:36:40.264Z",codex-agent,"Caller-adoption update: the newly published 2026.10.27 release at tag commit f90f86faa9c976392f1d1262fd0b3204de2007e4 retains byte-identical closeout.ts, index.ts, import-fidelity.ts and both reusable workflows from original main 2b71f73. Bumping to that release does not fix this incident. All 21 callers listed in docs/scheduled-workflow-refusals.md need a release SHA containing PR #190. Explicit required-check declarations and the documented pm-changelog source-content privacy remediation remain caller-owned. Source and re-review class fixes now pass both complete local release gates, 1548/1548 each with exact all-source four-dimensional coverage; PR #190 remains open for verification and is not merged."
  "2026-10-29T19:41:40.800Z",codex-agent,"2026-10-29 daily-sync follow-up from pm-github-3it2 / companion pm-cli-website-c0jw: after the package release, adopt pins through Dependabot; caller-owned issues:write grant is also needed for failure-issue creation/update/recovery closure (a reusable workflow cannot raise issues:read). Source-content triage is in docs/daily-sync-recovery.md: seven policy-refusal issue bodies across six repositories, including synthetic examples, remain for orchestrator remediation. pm-csv issue #197 separately has multiple existing owners and needs provenance repair. No fleet callers or source-content records were edited by this package work."
  "2026-11-06T22:43:42.194Z",codex-agent,"Investigating the November 6 scheduled-workflow watch via REST job summaries and bounded log samples. Separating caller pin adoption, duplicate provenance, tracker validation, repeat-import drift and closeout failures. Replays use disposable public caller clones with their pinned SDK and both their workflow release and 2026.11.4. No caller workflow edits or remote apply operations are authorized."
  "2026-11-06T22:59:10.678Z",codex-agent,"The watch contains 21 sync and 15 closeout failures across 22 callers. Shared release normalization and no-op fixes are already in published 2026.11.4. pm-slack replay confirms its issue #159 changes the pm-slack-77v5 item/history on the second import with 2026.10.28, while 2026.11.4 repeats with zero durable changes on the same pinned SDK. Duplicate provenance in pm-beads and required-create fields in pm-changelog still refuse on both releases. pm-ops still refuses its configured completeness policies (old close missing repro_steps, expected_result, resolution; latest update missing repro_steps). Caller data/policy remediation must retain these refusals."
  "2026-11-06T23:06:17.306Z",codex-agent,"Caller follow-up matrix is complete in docs/scheduled-workflow-watch-1106.md. All 22 callers need newer workflow pins for the shared changes; duplicate-owner remediation remains for pm-beads, pm-brief, pm-memory and pm-rl; required-create policy remains for pm-changelog; completeness data/policy remains for pm-ops; one source-body host-path refusal remains for pm-jev. The deprecated version input is warning-only (present in every watched caller except pm-glossary), and all 21 sync callers grant only issues:read, so failure-issue alerts additionally require caller-owned issues:write. No caller PRs were opened."
  "2026-11-07T07:00:57.492Z",codex-agent,"Review finding addressed at the class level: the live adoption description now links the November 6 watch matrix (22 callers), and README's operator entry point links the same current matrix alongside the historical guide. The package search found no other live adoption entry point that still directs operators solely to the historical 21-caller scope; closed historical incident records retain their execution context. A regression checks both live entry points and all 22 matrix rows."
  "2026-11-07T07:26:49.549Z",codex-agent,"Corrected a tracker mistake introduced in the first task round: the rollout follow-up had been given the canonical gh:unbraind/pm-github#175 ownership tag even though pm-github-repeat-noop already owns that issue. This item tracks dependent caller adoption, not the original defect's ownership. Removed only this item's duplicate tag using pinned pm; retained all history and the canonical owner's tag. A regression prevents rollout follow-ups from taking the canonical issue owner's provenance."
  "2026-11-07T09:14:01.802Z",codex-agent,"Clarified the watch matrix: the sync-only refusals in pm-beads and pm-memory require duplicate-owner repair, pm-ops requires configured completeness data/policy repair, and pm-jev requires source privacy remediation or a reviewed narrow allowlist. Both old and current releases refuse these cases, so a newer pin is recommended for diagnostics but is not their demonstrated cure. The other eighteen callers exhibit at least one release-fixed install, repeat-import or pagination class and need pin adoption; pm-brief, pm-rl and pm-changelog additionally need their documented caller repairs. This supersedes the earlier blanket statement that all twenty-two require a pin to resolve their observed refusal."
  "2026-11-14T08:49:18.379Z",codex-sweep-1114,"2026-11-14 sweep: returned idle or paused work to open; no agent is actively working this item. Delivered slices: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/190 merged 2026-10-29T02:48:01Z; merge SHA 4deec2a0a24d1bcdefdf0f35294588515569aeae; PR head 9734d424af08128453908df8ad66ac6b0e963509. Delivered: Coordinate caller adoption and source-content remediation for scheduled workflows. Green at that head: test (22), codeql, test (26), bun-release (22), bun-release (26), CodeQL, CodeRabbit, semgrep-cloud-platform/scan. Other check outcomes: enable-auto-merge: SKIPPED; cubic · AI code reviewer: NEUTRAL; Sourcery review: SKIPPED (not counted as green). https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/198 merged 2026-10-30T08:48:28Z; merge SHA 4568f2e8e2a349738e9e55900e4572ca7fe6994a; PR head 4288901fc1df88f17bab46216db2de387ca31899. Delivered: Coordinate caller adoption and source-content remediation for scheduled workflows. Green at that head: test (22), codeql, test (26), bun-release (22), bun-release (26), CodeQL, CodeRabbit, cubic · AI code reviewer, semgrep-cloud-platform/scan. Other check outcomes: enable-auto-merge: SKIPPED; Sourcery review: SKIPPED (not counted as green). https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/225 merged 2026-11-07T10:49:25Z; merge SHA 0e070fa97ca53a865d1979375a8a603cd0245cd3; PR head 853b86871a5ae4de09027285b7b2faaabcb05cac. Delivered: Coordinate caller adoption and source-content remediation for scheduled workflows. Green at that head: test (22), codeql, test (26), bun-release (22), bun-release (26), CodeQL, CodeRabbit, Greptile Review, Sourcery review, semgrep-cloud-platform/scan. Other check outcomes: verified-auto-merge: SKIPPED; verified-auto-merge: SKIPPED; verified-auto-merge: SKIPPED; audit-armed-requests: SKIPPED; audit-armed-requests: SKIPPED; audit-armed-requests: SKIPPED; cubic · AI code reviewer: NEUTRAL (not counted as green). Remaining: caller owners must adopt verified workflow pins, repair required-check/provenance/privacy inputs and validate real scheduled GITHUB_TOKEN runs across the documented caller matrix. Package diagnostics and replay documentation alone do not deliver that rollout."
